{"path":"3/library/platform.html","title":"platform — Access to underlying platform’s identifying data","description":"Source code: Lib/platform.py","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"module-platform"},{"type":"anchor","id":"platform-access-to-underlying-platform-s-identifying-data"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"platform"},{"type":"text","value":" — Access to underlying platform’s identifying data"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source code:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/python/cpython/tree/3.14/Lib/platform.py","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lib/platform.py"}]}]},{"type":"thematic_break"},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specific platforms listed alphabetically, with Linux included in the Unix section."}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"cross-platform"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cross platform"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.architecture","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.architecture("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"executable"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"sys.executable"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"bits"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"linkage"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Queries the given executable (defaults to the Python interpreter binary) for various architecture information."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a tuple "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(bits, linkage)"},{"type":"text","value":" which contain information about the bit architecture and the linkage format used for the executable. Both values are returned as strings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Values that cannot be determined are returned as given by the parameter presets. If bits is given as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"''"},{"type":"text","value":", the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sizeof(pointer)"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sizeof(long)"},{"type":"text","value":" on Python version < 1.5.2) is used as indicator for the supported pointer size."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function relies on the system’s "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"file"},{"type":"text","value":" command to do the actual work. This is available on most if not all Unix platforms and some non-Unix platforms and then only if the executable points to the Python interpreter. Reasonable defaults are used when the above needs are not met."}]},{"type":"admonition","kind":"note","title":"Note","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On macOS (and perhaps other platforms), executable files may be universal files containing multiple architectures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To get at the “64-bitness” of the current interpreter, it is more reliable to query the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/sys.html#sys.maxsize","title":"sys.maxsize","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"sys.maxsize"}]},{"type":"text","value":" attribute:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":"is_64bits = sys.maxsize > 2**32"}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.machine","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.machine()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the machine type, e.g. "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'AMD64'"},{"type":"text","value":". An empty string is returned if the value cannot be determined."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The output is platform-dependent and may differ in casing and naming conventions."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.node","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.node()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the computer’s network name (may not be fully qualified!). An empty string is returned if the value cannot be determined."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.platform","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.platform("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"aliased"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"False"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"terse"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"False"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a single string identifying the underlying platform with as much useful information as possible."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The output is intended to be "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"human readable"}]},{"type":"text","value":" rather than machine parseable. It may look different on different platforms and this is intended."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"aliased"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is true, the function will use aliases for various platforms that report system names which differ from their common names, for example SunOS will be reported as Solaris. The "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.system_alias","title":"platform.system_alias","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"system_alias()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function is used to implement this."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Setting "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"terse"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to true causes the function to return only the absolute minimum information needed to identify the platform."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.8: On macOS, the function now uses "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.mac_ver","title":"platform.mac_ver","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"mac_ver()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", if it returns a non-empty release string, to get the macOS version rather than the darwin version."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.processor","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.processor()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the (real) processor name, e.g. "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'amdk6'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An empty string is returned if the value cannot be determined. Note that many platforms do not provide this information or simply return the same value as for "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.machine","title":"platform.machine","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"machine()"}]},{"type":"text","value":". NetBSD does this."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.python_build","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.python_build()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a tuple "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(buildno, builddate)"},{"type":"text","value":" stating the Python build number and date as strings."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.python_compiler","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.python_compiler()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a string identifying the compiler used for compiling Python."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.python_branch","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.python_branch()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a string identifying the Python implementation SCM branch."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.python_implementation","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.python_implementation()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a string identifying the Python implementation. Possible return values are: ‘CPython’, ‘IronPython’, ‘Jython’, ‘PyPy’."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.python_revision","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.python_revision()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a string identifying the Python implementation SCM revision."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.python_version","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.python_version()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the Python version as string "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'major.minor.patchlevel'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that unlike the Python "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sys.version"},{"type":"text","value":", the returned value will always include the patchlevel (it defaults to 0)."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.python_version_tuple","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.python_version_tuple()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the Python version as tuple "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(major, minor, patchlevel)"},{"type":"text","value":" of strings."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that unlike the Python "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sys.version"},{"type":"text","value":", the returned value will always include the patchlevel (it defaults to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'0'"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.release","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.release()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the system’s release, e.g. "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'2.2.0'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'NT'"},{"type":"text","value":". An empty string is returned if the value cannot be determined."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.system","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.system()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the system/OS name, such as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Linux'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Darwin'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Java'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Windows'"},{"type":"text","value":". An empty string is returned if the value cannot be determined."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On iOS and Android, this returns the user-facing OS name (i.e, "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'iOS"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'iPadOS'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Android'"},{"type":"text","value":"). To obtain the kernel name ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Darwin'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Linux'"},{"type":"text","value":"), use "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/os.html#os.uname","title":"os.uname","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"os.uname()"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.system_alias","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.system_alias("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"system"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"release"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"version"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(system, release, version)"},{"type":"text","value":" aliased to common marketing names used for some systems. It also does some reordering of the information in some cases where it would otherwise cause confusion."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.version","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.version()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns the system’s release version, e.g. "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'#3 on degas'"},{"type":"text","value":". An empty string is returned if the value cannot be determined."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On iOS and Android, this is the user-facing OS version. To obtain the Darwin or Linux kernel version, use "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/os.html#os.uname","title":"os.uname","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"os.uname()"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.uname","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.uname()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fairly portable uname interface. Returns a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/collections.html#collections.namedtuple","title":"collections.namedtuple","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"namedtuple()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" containing six attributes: "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.system","title":"platform.system","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"system"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.node","title":"platform.node","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"node"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.release","title":"platform.release","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"release"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.version","title":"platform.version","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"version"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.machine","title":"platform.machine","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"machine"}]},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.processor","title":"platform.processor","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"processor"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.processor","title":"platform.processor","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"processor"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is resolved late, on demand."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note: the first two attribute names differ from the names presented by "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/os.html#os.uname","title":"os.uname","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"os.uname()"}]},{"type":"text","value":", where they are named "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"sysname"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"nodename"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entries which cannot be determined are set to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"''"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.3: Result changed from a tuple to a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/collections.html#collections.namedtuple","title":"collections.namedtuple","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"namedtuple()"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changed in version 3.9: "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.processor","title":"platform.processor","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"processor"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is resolved late instead of immediately."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.invalidate_caches","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.invalidate_caches()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Clear out the internal cache of information, such as the "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.uname","title":"platform.uname","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"uname()"}]},{"type":"text","value":". This is typically useful when the platform’s "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.node","title":"platform.node","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"node()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is changed by an external process and one needs to retrieve the updated value."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.14."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"java-platform"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Java platform"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.java_ver","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.java_ver("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"release"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"vendor"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"vminfo"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"('', "},{"type":"text","value":"'', "},{"type":"text","value":"'')"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"osinfo"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"('', "},{"type":"text","value":"'', "},{"type":"text","value":"'')"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version interface for Jython."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a tuple "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(release, vendor, vminfo, osinfo)"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"vminfo"}]},{"type":"text","value":" being a tuple "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(vm_name, vm_release, vm_vendor)"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"osinfo"}]},{"type":"text","value":" being a tuple "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(os_name, os_version, os_arch)"},{"type":"text","value":". Values which cannot be determined are set to the defaults given as parameters (which all default to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"''"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated since version 3.13, will be removed in version 3.15: It was largely untested, had a confusing API, and was only useful for Jython support."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"windows-platform"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Windows platform"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.win32_ver","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.win32_ver("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"release"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"version"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"csd"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ptype"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get additional version information from the Windows Registry and return a tuple "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(release, version, csd, ptype)"},{"type":"text","value":" referring to OS release, version number, CSD level (service pack) and OS type (multi/single processor). Values which cannot be determined are set to the defaults given as parameters (which all default to an empty string)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"As a hint: "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ptype"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Uniprocessor Free'"},{"type":"text","value":" on single processor NT machines and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Multiprocessor Free'"},{"type":"text","value":" on multi processor machines. The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Free'"},{"type":"text","value":" refers to the OS version being free of debugging code. It could also state "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Checked'"},{"type":"text","value":" which means the OS version uses debugging code, i.e. code that checks arguments, ranges, etc."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.win32_edition","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.win32_edition()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns a string representing the current Windows edition, or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"None"},{"type":"text","value":" if the value cannot be determined. Possible values include but are not limited to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'Enterprise'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'IoTUAP'"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'ServerStandard'"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'nanoserver'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.8."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.win32_is_iot","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.win32_is_iot()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Return "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"True"},{"type":"text","value":" if the Windows edition returned by "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.win32_edition","title":"platform.win32_edition","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"win32_edition()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" is recognized as an IoT edition."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.8."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"macos-platform"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"macOS platform"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.mac_ver","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.mac_ver("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"release"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"versioninfo"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"('', "},{"type":"text","value":"'', "},{"type":"text","value":"'')"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"machine"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get macOS version information and return it as tuple "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(release, versioninfo,\nmachine)"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"versioninfo"}]},{"type":"text","value":" being a tuple "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(version, dev_stage,\nnon_release_version)"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entries which cannot be determined are set to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"''"},{"type":"text","value":". All tuple entries are strings."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"ios-platform"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"iOS platform"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.ios_ver","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.ios_ver("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"system"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"release"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"is_simulator"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"False"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get iOS version information and return it as a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/collections.html#collections.namedtuple","title":"collections.namedtuple","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"namedtuple()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the following attributes:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"system"},{"type":"text","value":" is the OS name; either "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'iOS'"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'iPadOS'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"release"},{"type":"text","value":" is the iOS version number as a string (e.g., "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'17.2'"},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" is the device model identifier; this will be a string like "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'iPhone13,2'"},{"type":"text","value":" for a physical device, or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'iPhone'"},{"type":"text","value":" on a simulator."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"is_simulator"},{"type":"text","value":" is a boolean describing if the app is running on a simulator or a physical device."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Entries which cannot be determined are set to the defaults given as parameters."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"unix-platforms"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unix platforms"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.libc_ver","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.libc_ver("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"executable"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"sys.executable"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"lib"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"version"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"chunksize"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"16384"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tries to determine the libc version against which the file executable (defaults to the Python interpreter) is linked. Returns a tuple of strings "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"(lib,\nversion)"},{"type":"text","value":" which default to the given parameters in case the lookup fails."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that this function has intimate knowledge of how different libc versions add symbols to the executable is probably only usable for executables compiled using "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"gcc"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The file is read and scanned in chunks of "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"chunksize"}]},{"type":"text","value":" bytes."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"linux-platforms"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Linux platforms"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.freedesktop_os_release","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.freedesktop_os_release()"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get operating system identification from "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"os-release"},{"type":"text","value":" file and return it as a dict. The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"os-release"},{"type":"text","value":" file is a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/os-release.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"freedesktop.org standard"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and is available in most Linux distributions. A noticeable exception is Android and Android-based distributions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Raises "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/exceptions.html#OSError","title":"OSError","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"OSError"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or subclass when neither "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/etc/os-release"},{"type":"text","value":" nor "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"/usr/lib/os-release"},{"type":"text","value":" can be read."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On success, the function returns a dictionary where keys and values are strings. Values have their special characters like "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\""},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"$"},{"type":"text","value":" unquoted. The fields "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NAME"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"ID"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"PRETTY_NAME"},{"type":"text","value":" are always defined according to the standard. All other fields are optional. Vendors may include additional fields."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that fields like "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"NAME"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"VERSION"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"VARIANT"},{"type":"text","value":" are strings suitable for presentation to users. Programs should use fields like "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"ID"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"ID_LIKE"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"VERSION_ID"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"VARIANT_ID"},{"type":"text","value":" to identify Linux distributions."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":"def get_like_distro():\n    info = platform.freedesktop_os_release()\n    ids = [info[\"ID\"]]\n    if \"ID_LIKE\" in info:\n        # ids are space separated and ordered by precedence\n        ids.extend(info[\"ID_LIKE\"].split())\n    return ids"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.10."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"android-platform"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Android platform"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"platform.android_ver","term":[{"type":"text","value":"platform.android_ver("},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"release"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"api_level"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"0"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"manufacturer"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"model"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"device"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"''"}]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"is_emulator"},{"type":"text","value":"="},{"type":"text","value":"False"}]},{"type":"text","value":")"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Get Android device information. Returns a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/collections.html#collections.namedtuple","title":"collections.namedtuple","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"namedtuple()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the following attributes. Values which cannot be determined are set to the defaults given as parameters."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"release"},{"type":"text","value":" - Android version, as a string (e.g. "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"\"14\""},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"api_level"},{"type":"text","value":" - API level of the running device, as an integer (e.g. "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"34"},{"type":"text","value":" for Android 14). To get the API level which Python was built against, see "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/sys.html#sys.getandroidapilevel","title":"sys.getandroidapilevel","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"sys.getandroidapilevel()"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"manufacturer"},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"link","href":"https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Build#MANUFACTURER","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Manufacturer name"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"model"},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"link","href":"https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Build#MODEL","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model name"}]},{"type":"text","value":" – typically the marketing name or model number."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"device"},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"link","href":"https://developer.android.com/reference/android/os/Build#DEVICE","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Device name"}]},{"type":"text","value":" – typically the model number or a codename."}]}]},{"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"is_emulator"},{"type":"text","value":" - "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"True"},{"type":"text","value":" if the device is an emulator; "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"False"},{"type":"text","value":" if it’s a physical device."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Google maintains a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://storage.googleapis.com/play_public/supported_devices.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"list of known model and device names"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Added in version 3.13."}]}]}]},{"type":"anchor","id":"command-line-usage"},{"type":"anchor","id":"platform-cli"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Command-line usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"platform"},{"type":"text","value":" can also be invoked directly using the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://docs.python.org/3/using/cmdline.html#cmdoption-m","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"-m"}]},{"type":"text","value":" switch of the interpreter:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"python","code":"python -m platform [--terse] [--nonaliased] [{nonaliased,terse} ...]"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following options are accepted:"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"cmdoption-platform-terse","term":[{"type":"text","value":"--terse"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Print terse information about the platform. This is equivalent to calling "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.platform","title":"platform.platform","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"platform.platform()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"terse"}]},{"type":"text","value":" argument set to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"True"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":"cmdoption-platform-nonaliased","term":[{"type":"text","value":"--nonaliased"}],"definition":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Print platform information without system/OS name aliasing. This is equivalent to calling "},{"type":"link","href":"3/library/platform.html#platform.platform","title":"platform.platform","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"platform.platform()"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"aliased"}]},{"type":"text","value":" argument set to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"True"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also pass one or more positional arguments ("},{"type":"inline_code","code":"terse"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"nonaliased"},{"type":"text","value":") to explicitly control the output format. These behave similarly to their corresponding options."}]}]}}
